{"causes": ["The Portuguese Empire's aggressive expansionist policies in Asia aimed to secure strategic trading posts and convert local populations to Catholicism.", "The 1591 Portuguese expedition to Jaffna, led by André Furtado de Mendonça, resulted in the assassination of King Puviraja Pandaram, creating a power vacuum.", "Internal factionalism and the perceived weakness of the Jaffna Kingdom provided an opportune moment for foreign intervention and the imposition of suzerainty."], "effects": ["Ethirimanna Cinkam's reign solidified Portuguese influence over the Jaffna Kingdom through tribute payments and the establishment of Catholic missions.", "His death in 1617 led to a succession crisis that directly facilitated the full annexation of the Jaffna Kingdom by the Portuguese in 1619.", "The end of the Aryacakravarti dynasty under his successor marked the cessation of an independent Tamil kingdom in northern Sri Lanka for over 300 years."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "portuguese-conquest-of-jaffna", "sourceName": "Portuguese Conquest of Jaffna", "verb": "CAUSES", "targetSlug": "ethirimana-cinkam", "targetName": "Ethirimana Cinkam", "context": "The 1591 Portuguese expedition directly led to Ethirimana Cinkam's installation as king under Portuguese suzerainty."}, {"sourceSlug": "ethirimana-cinkam", "sourceName": "Ethirimana Cinkam", "verb": "SUCCEEDS", "targetSlug": "puviraja-pandaram", "targetName": "Puviraja Pandaram", "context": "Ethirimanna Cinkam ascended to the throne of the Jaffna Kingdom following the assassination of his father, Puviraja Pandaram, in 1591."}, {"sourceSlug": "ethirimana-cinkam", "sourceName": "Ethirimana Cinkam", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "jaffna-kingdom", "targetName": "Jaffna Kingdom", "context": "Ethirimanna Cinkam ruled as king within the geographical and political boundaries of the Jaffna Kingdom from 1591 to 1617."}, {"sourceSlug": "ethirimana-cinkam", "sourceName": "Ethirimana Cinkam", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug"